{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>How many are the days of the years of your life?</b> It seemed to him that he was far older than the rest of the men of his generation, and therefore he asked him thus. And Jacob answered: <b>The days of the years of my sojournings</b> — he did not say 'the years of my life,' as Pharaoh had mentioned, but rather 'my sojournings,' that is to say: the days in which I am a sojourner in this world are one hundred and thirty years. So is the way of the righteous, who reckon themselves sojourners in this world. But after he mentioned 'my sojournings,' he mentioned 'the days of the years of my life,' that is to say: my life has been one of suffering. But concerning his fathers, who did not have suffering as great, he mentioned 'life' first and afterward the expression of their sojournings."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:20:52.108432725Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}